## Why This Is Asked
Auditing and non-repudiation in CNF gateways are critical for multi-tenant environments. This question validates practical expertise with Kubernetes Secrets, HMAC signing, sidecar log pipelines, and retention configuration—essential skills for implementing post-deployment security controls.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped auditing and non-repudiation
- HMAC signing using per-tenant Kubernetes Secrets
- Sidecar-based log forwarding to in-cluster sinks
- ConfigMap-driven log retention and namespace scoping

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');
function signLog(logLine, secret) {
  return crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret)
    .update(logLine)
    .digest('hex');
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical design of end-to-end attestation workflows in multi-tenant environments with integrated policy enforcement and security controls.

## Key Concepts
- Post-deployment tenant-scoped attestations using HSM-based key management
- SBOM integrity verification and runtime hashing for supply chain security
- OPA/Gatekeeper integration for policy validation and traffic gating
- Multi-tenant security isolation with compliance enforcement mechanisms

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sample attestation verification pseudocode
function verifyAttestation(attestation, tenantPolicy) {
  // Validate signature with tenant's HSM public key
  const isValidSignature = crypto.verify(
    attestation.signature,
    attestation.payload,
    tenantPolicy.publicKey
  );

  // Check policy compliance through OPA/Gatekeeper
  const isCompliant = opa.evaluate(
    attestation.payload,
    tenantPolicy.constraints
  );

  return isValidSignature && isCompliant;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design tenant-aware rate limiting and observability in CNF gateways, a realistic production concern for multi-tenant platforms used by large companies.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped policy API (REST)
- Sidecar token bucket limiter with TTL cache
- Real-time policy fetch and rotation
- Central audit/log sink and schema

## Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, fillRate) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.fillRate = fillRate;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n = 1) {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.fillRate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

